<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 250 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 250 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 250 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN    =	    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    500 MLN    750 MLN    =	    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS	=	  250 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p>BILLS/FRG FEB 10/11  500 MLN!</p>
<p>*  INTEREST RATE OF 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INTEREST RATE OF 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
